DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     rrsshh is built from the same command-interpreter sources as
     sshh, compiled as a separate program from a copy of those
     sources kept under its own name; it accepts the same option
     letters and the same command language.  With no _f_i_l_e and
     without -cc or -ss, rrsshh reads commands from its standard in-
     put.  With a _f_i_l_e argument (and neither -cc nor -ss), rrsshh
     reads commands from _f_i_l_e, and any further arguments become
     that script's positional parameters.  With -cc, rrsshh executes
     _s_t_r_i_n_g as a command, and any further arguments become its
     positional parameters.

     Option letters may be combined after a single leading -, as
     in -eexx.

